course: dictionary
lesson: 8079
title: Rely on it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To rely on someone or something means you need them and can trust them to help you or to work. «Newborn puppies cannot see or hear for about the first two weeks and rely on smell, touch and their mother's warmth.» The puppies cannot manage alone, so rely shows they need those things to survive.
explain: Look for the little word after rely: «on». You rely on something, not just rely. Test your meaning by swapping in need or trust: «Actors rely on each other's lines» means actors need and trust each other to say the right words. If one forgets, the others are left stuck on stage.
explain: Rely can also mean you are sure something will happen. «You can rely on the bus to come at eight» means you are sure it will come. But you can't rely on a guess, so check it instead. Rely is a verb and changes its form: rely, relies, relied, relying.
fact: Rely is a verb, so its forms are rely, relies, relied and relying.
fact: Rely is nearly always used with «on» or «upon»: rely on someone, rely on something.
fact: «Rely» means to trust someone to help you, or to need something to work or to live.
fact: Relying on a guess is risky, so it is better to check.
fact: Useful phrases: rely on, can rely on, rely on each other, you can't rely on.
exercise: «Newborn puppies cannot see or hear for about the first two weeks and rely on smell, touch and their mother's warmth.» What do the puppies need? | Bright lights and loud music | Eight eyes to see with | *Smell, touch and their mother's warmth | A new home straight away
exercise: Ella says, «I can rely on my best friend.» What does rely on mean here? | *Trust her to help me | Wait for her to leave | Argue with her every day | Forget all about her
exercise: «Plants rely on sun, water and air.» What do plants need? | Other plants' leaves | *Sun, water and air | Nothing at all | Only sweets and biscuits
test: Which word completes the sentence? «Vets ___ on keepers' notes, weight and training.» | drooped | ancient | barely | *rely
test: Which word completes the sentence? «You can ___ on your best friend to help you.» | famished | luminous | *rely | curt
exam: Which is the best way to deal with a guess in maths? | Rely on the guess and move on | Write it in bigger letters | Ask a friend to rely on it for you | *Check it, because relying on a guess is risky
